admin-ssh-fetch = Inspect saved server's host key
admin-ssh-observed = Observed, untrusted host key
admin-ssh-confirm-pin = I verified this fingerprint through a trusted, separate channel
admin-ssh-use-pin = Add verified key to this draft
admin-ssh-targets = Allowed destinations
admin-ssh-target-host = Destination hostname
admin-ssh-target-port = Destination port
admin-ssh-target-private = Allow this destination on a private or loopback address
admin-ssh-add-target = Add destination
admin-ssh-remove-target = Remove destination
admin-ssh-target-help = Only these exact host and port pairs can be opened. Addresses are resolved and checked locally, then pinned for the SSH channel. Metadata and other unsafe destinations remain blocked.
admin-ssh-limits = Connection limits
admin-ssh-keepalive = Keepalive interval (seconds)
admin-ssh-timeout = Connection timeout (milliseconds)
admin-ssh-channels = Maximum channels
admin-ssh-save = Save tunnel
admin-ssh-test = Test saved connection and first destination
admin-ssh-saved-only = Save changes before inspecting or testing. Diagnostics always use the saved configuration.
admin-ssh-test-ok = The saved SSH connection authenticated and opened the first allowed destination.
admin-ssh-test-failed = The saved connection test failed. Review its phase, host-key pins, credential and destination policy.
admin-ssh-phase = Diagnostic phase
admin-ssh-code = Diagnostic result code
admin-ssh-elapsed = Elapsed time
admin-ssh-empty = No SSH tunnels configured.
admin-ssh-missing = This SSH tunnel no longer exists.
admin-ssh-status = Status
admin-ssh-active = Enabled
admin-ssh-disabled = Disabled
admin-ssh-remove = Remove tunnel
admin-ssh-remove-title = Remove SSH tunnel?
admin-ssh-remove-detail = Connections referencing this tunnel will stop working. They will not fall back to direct access.
admin-ssh-no-manage = You can view this tunnel, but cannot change it.
admin-ssh-review-title = Review credential authority change
admin-ssh-review-body = This changes the SSH server, login identity or trusted host keys while retaining the sealed credential. Confirm the new authority before allowing that credential to authenticate there.
admin-ssh-review-confirm = Confirm authority and save
admin-ssh-review-old = Previously saved server
admin-ssh-review-new = New server

admin-ssh-review-old-pins = Previously trusted host keys
admin-ssh-review-new-pins = New trusted host keys

admin-ssh-refresh = Refresh

admin-ssh-validation-title = Check these tunnel settings
admin-ssh-validation-name = Enter a tunnel name of at most 128 bytes.
admin-ssh-validation-host = Enter a hostname or IP address, without ssh://, a username, a path or a port.
admin-ssh-validation-port = SSH port must be a whole number from 1 to 65535.
admin-ssh-validation-user = Enter an SSH username of at most 128 bytes.
admin-ssh-validation-keepalive = Keepalive must be 10–300 seconds.
admin-ssh-validation-timeout = Connection timeout must be 100–60000 milliseconds.
admin-ssh-validation-channels = Concurrent channels must be a whole number from 1 to 128.
admin-ssh-validation-pin = Add up to 16 valid SHA256 host-key fingerprints with supported algorithms.
admin-ssh-validation-target = Add up to 128 unique destination hostname/port pairs with valid ports.
admin-ssh-validation-enabled = Before enabling, add a trusted host key and at least one allowed destination.
admin-ssh-fetch-current = Fetch current host key
admin-ssh-fetch-current-help = Contact the hostname and port in this draft without sending credentials. Review the returned fingerprint before trusting it.
admin-ssh-tofu-help = SSH identifies servers by host keys, not TLS certificates. You can verify a fingerprint separately, or explicitly trust the first key observed (TOFU). Once saved, a different key is rejected. TOFU cannot verify who owns the server on the first connection.
admin-ssh-tofu-confirm = Trust this first observed key (TOFU); I accept the first-connection identity risk
admin-ssh-tofu-add = Trust first key in this draft
admin-ssh-key-changed = This key differs from the trusted fingerprints. Verify the change separately before adding it. Trust on first use cannot replace an existing key.
